From: ProAudio Player <noreply@proaudio-player.local>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 20:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] spotifyd: restart cleanly after malformed discovery handshake

Spotify Android can occasionally send an empty addUser blob after a stale
zeroconf handshake. librespot 0.8.0 returns HmacError in that case, but the
HTTP request task then panics while the discovery server and spotifyd process
can remain alive. Subsequent attempts keep using the stale server key and fail
until spotifyd is restarted.

A valid encrypted blob needs a 16-byte IV and a 20-byte checksum in addition
to any encrypted payload. Reject every blob shorter than 36 bytes before the
subsequent slices are formed.

Discovery already has a ServerError event whose documented behavior is to
terminate the credential stream. Emit that event before returning the existing
error. Also treat a terminated discovery stream as fatal while an existing
Spotify session is active. The spotifyd process then exits and systemd starts a
fresh receiver with a new discovery key.

The initial, not-yet-connected path already exits when the discovery stream
closes, so together these changes cover both startup and active-session cases.
Invalid credential data is still rejected; this patch does not relax any
cryptographic validation.
---
 VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs |  8 ++++++--
 src/main_loop.rs                          | 12 ++++++++----
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs b/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
+++ b/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
@@ -157,8 +157,12 @@ impl RequestHandler {
         let shared_key = self.keys.shared_secret(&client_key);
 
         let encrypted_blob_len = encrypted_blob.len();
-        if encrypted_blob_len < 16 {
-            return Err(DiscoveryError::HmacError(encrypted_blob.to_vec()).into());
+        if encrypted_blob_len < 36 {
+            let blob = encrypted_blob.to_vec();
+            let _ = self.event_tx.send(DiscoveryEvent::ServerError(
+                DiscoveryError::HmacError(blob.clone()),
+            ));
+            return Err(DiscoveryError::HmacError(blob).into());
         }
 
         let iv = &encrypted_blob[0..16];
diff --git a/src/main_loop.rs b/src/main_loop.rs
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/main_loop.rs
+++ b/src/main_loop.rs
@@ -52,15 +52,15 @@ impl CredentialsProvider {
         }
     }
 
-    // wait for an incoming connection if the underlying provider is a discovery stream
-    async fn incoming_connection(&mut self) {
+    // Wait for an incoming connection. `true` means discovery terminated and
+    // the receiver must be restarted to obtain a fresh zeroconf server key.
+    async fn incoming_connection(&mut self) -> bool {
         match self {
             CredentialsProvider::Discovery { stream, .. } => {
                 let peeked = Pin::new(stream).peek().await;
-                if peeked.is_none() {
-                    future::pending().await
-                }
+                peeked.is_none()
             }
-            _ => future::pending().await,
+            _ => future::pending::<bool>().await,
         }
     }
 }
@@ -204,7 +204,11 @@ impl MainLoop {
             loop {
                 tokio::select!(
                     // a new session has been started via the discovery stream
-                    _ = self.credentials_provider.incoming_connection() => {
+                    discovery_closed = self.credentials_provider.incoming_connection() => {
+                        if discovery_closed {
+                            break 'mainloop Err(eyre::eyre!("Spotify discovery stream terminated"));
+                        }
                         let _ = shared_spirc.shutdown();
                         let _ = (&mut spirc_task).await;
                         break;
-- 
